meta {
  name: Create Channel - Full Featured
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/channels
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Channel Full",
    "format": "CSV",
    "product_list_id": "6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb",
    "rebuild_periodically": true,
    "rebuild_feed_frequency": "DAILY",
    "rebuild_feed_hod": 3,
    "rebuild_feed_moh": 0,
    "rebuild_feed_timezone": "UTC"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.product_list_id: eq 6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb
  res.body.data.rebuild_periodically: eq true
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture
  kept** -- id `6aa047d52b6fd055ffb7cadd`, for Phase 5's end-to-end flows.

  `201 Created`. `product_list_id` (Phase 3a's kept Smart list) links
  immediately on create -- same as products (Phase 2b), unlike assets
  (Phase 2a). `rebuild_feed_next_build` gets computed automatically
  (`"2026-09-09T03:00:00+00:00"`, matching the `hod`/`moh`/`timezone`
  sent). `active` also auto-flips to `true` once a complete rebuild
  schedule is set, even though it wasn't sent in the request.

  ## Opaque validation error for incomplete rebuild scheduling
  `rebuild_periodically: true` **alone** (or with `rebuild_feed_frequency`
  but missing `rebuild_feed_hod`/`rebuild_feed_moh`/
  `rebuild_feed_timezone`) fails with a **vague, field-less** error:
  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"Schema
  validation error"}]}` -- no indication of which field is missing,
  unlike every other 422 confirmed in this project (which all name the
  specific field). Confirmed via elimination: `rebuild_feed_frequency`
  works fine on its own (round-trips, just inert while
  `rebuild_periodically` stays `false`); it's specifically turning
  `rebuild_periodically` on without also supplying `hod`/`moh`/`timezone`
  together that triggers this opaque failure. Worth flagging to Plytix --
  this is measurably worse error-message quality than the rest of the API.

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  Channel names are unique per account. Re-running once the fixture
  exists returns `409 Conflict {"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists",
  "description":"A channel with the same name already exists"}]}` --
  same `409`/`AlreadyExists` family as attribute groups/attributes/
  products, not lists' `422` family (`config/api-testing.config.md`
  quirk #45a).
}
